    "repro_summary": "The reproducer tests the use-after-free race condition in the Energy Model (EM) code where a reader thread accesses `dev->em_pd` after a writer thread frees it.",
    "result_summary": "The baseline reproduced the EM use-after-free bug (KASAN splat in `reader_fn+0xa0/0xb0`), while the patched build was clean.",
    "detail": "## Analysis\n\n### 1. What the reproducer does\n\nThe reproducer (`em_uaf_repro.ko`) creates two kthreads pinned to separate CPUs:\n\n- **Reader** (CPU 0): fetches a raw `struct em_perf_domain *` via `em_pd_get()`, waits 5 \u00b5s, then dereferences `pd->nr_perf_states`:\n\n```c\nstruct em_perf_domain *pd = em_pd_get(dev);\nif (pd) {\n    udelay(5);\n    WRITE_ONCE(pd->nr_perf_states, pd->nr_perf_states);\n}\n```\n\n- **Writer** (CPU 1): loops calling `em_dev_unregister_perf_domain()` (which `kfree()`s the struct) followed by `em_dev_register_perf_domain()` (which allocates a new one), with `msleep(1)` to prevent RCU callback OOM:\n\n```c\nem_dev_unregister_perf_domain(dev);\nret = em_dev_register_perf_domain(dev, 4, &em_cb, NULL, true);\nmsleep(1);\n```\n\nThe bug is that `em_pd_get()` returns a raw pointer with no RCU protection, so the writer can `kfree()` the struct between the reader's fetch and dereference.\n\n### 2. What happened: bug reproduced\n\nThe KASAN splat appears at `[  187.734733]` in the serial console (baseline variant), confirming the use-after-free:\n\n```\n[  187.735407] BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in reader_fn+0xa0/0xb0 [em_uaf_repro]\n[  187.736866] Read of size 4 at addr fff0000011858d1c by task em_uaf_reader/988\n```\n\nThe freed object belongs to `kmalloc-64` \u2014 the `struct em_perf_domain`:\n\n```\n[  187.744686] The buggy address belongs to the object at fff0000011858d00\n[  187.744686]  which belongs to the cache kmalloc-64 of size 64\n[  187.744865] The buggy address is located 28 bytes inside of\n[  187.744865]  freed 64-byte region [fff0000011858d00, fff0000011858d40)\n```\n\nThe call trace points directly to the reader's dereference:\n\n```\n[  187.740590]  reader_fn+0xa0/0xb0 [em_uaf_repro]\n```\n\nAllocation and free are both by task 987 (the writer):\n\n```\n[  187.743224] Allocated by task 987:\n[  187.743280] Freed by task 987:\n```\n\nThe orchestrator log confirms this is the **baseline** (unfixed) result \u2014 it exited 0 because KASAN reports don't crash the kernel, and the harness detected the splat from the serial console. The **patched** variant ran cleanly (exit 0, no splat), confirming the RCU fix works.",
    "source_url": null,
    "title": null,
    "short_title": "EM UAF",
    "summary_meta": "{\"detail\":{\"model\":\"opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\",\"ms\":30214,\"tokens\":293,\"took\":\"30s\"},\"repro\":{\"model\":\"opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\",\"ms\":8604,\"tokens\":25,\"took\":\"9s\"},\"result\":{\"model\":\"opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\",\"ms\":10405,\"tokens\":17,\"took\":\"10s\"},\"title\":{\"model\":\"opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\",\"ms\":9204,\"tokens\":2,\"took\":\"9s\"}}",
